 is to play as well as he  can to get someone else interested in  giving trubisky a chance for 2021. much  like carson wentz he may just need a  change of scenery but i'm not ready to  say neggy ruined the season he did what  he thought was right under the  circumstances i don't know that they  would have been much better with  trubisky playing i think this was a  total failure of the offense in recent  weeks they've tried to do some different  things it's too late for that but i feel  like they were destined to lose all  those games even if they had stuck with  trubisky new york nick asks this  question does home field advantage in  the playoffs matter in 2020 shireen  well  what is the difference between playing  in new orleans in a dome in green bay  outside so i would say absolutely yes  the bigger thing even than that mike  though is getting that first round bye  since there's only one of them this year  i think it's vitally important to get  the number one seed to have home field  and as rodney's going to talk about as i  alluded to earlier aaron rodgers hasn't  had that championship game at home and  can you imagine green bay even without  fans in january with aaron rodgers and  probably a snowy game that would be a  lot of fun but new orleans wants to be  in a dome of course and they want to get  that home field for just that reason  yeah i remember  a playoff game at home 2011 where the  packers had been 15-1 heavily favored  over the giants and they blew that i  just think they've got the propensity  to have a stinker at some point in the  playoffs even if they end up with the  one seed  those two games there's a chance that  after the fact much like what you said  earlier about sean payton the exact same  quotes from last year when they lost to  the falcons there's a card out there  that aaron rodgers has ready to go with  passive aggressive shots about the team  not having sufficient energy the team  not being ready to play the team not  being ready to execute without ever  saying who's the blame for that but we  all know who's to blame for the favor of  a team to prepare because sean payton  admits it's the coach when that happens  but that that's where my my doubt is and  i hope  and in a look i don't want to be  picking favorites here but man i'd love  to see aaron rodgers and patrick mahomes  in the super bowl that would be  compelling that would be exciting i  don't know that the packers could beat  the chiefs but it would be great to see  that match up but first the packers have  to get there whether they have the home  field advantage or not i think that you  can you can count on the possibility of  the packers blowing it at home but  otherwise it's not the same as the home  field advantage would be in other years  because there's no crowd there and one  thing we've seen in record numbers this  season come backs from 10 or more points  behind because if you're the road team  there's no noise to deal with as you try  to come back and if you're the home team  there's no booing to deal with as you  try to come back as your fans are all  upset that you've played so poorly so  that could be a factor in the postseason  as well one more real quickly j.r the  boss man  does the brown's performance without  otto beckham make it more likely that  he'll be traded in the off-season  shireen  well they've certainly been good without  and mike and they have proved our point  that we thought they were going to be a  better offense without him and they are  it allows them to run the ball which  they're really good at  takes the ball out of baker's hands and  he spread the ball around four  touchdowns last week to four different  receivers i think they're better without  odell beckham  yeah and if you have any doubt about  that because i've i've said all along  they'd be better off without him because  in the passing game you don't  have to focus on odell beckham jr and  maybe wait too long for him to come open  and not get 